  "body": "The Portal now submits complete coding task intent through the v2 command contract, journals the exact request before POST, restores all fields after reload, and rejects changed intent under a saved key. Accepted task cards read owner-scoped snapshots and display exact queue blockers. Historical saved requests remain available for exact retry.\n\nThe connected proof packet authenticates a real farmd browser session, checks unauthorized access and discovery after cache loss, and keeps credential-bearing diagnostics in private proof custody. Both forwarded and embedded Portal lanes use the same component worker and receipt subjects.\n\nValidation on dbb57bee978bb870555029e18cd14ea5b87e2413: full local required suite passed, including 258 unit tests, 14 mocked browser tests, bundle checks, lint, security and documentation. Independent review accepted the current source and exact inventory (13 new tests, none removed).\n\nRemaining blocker: earlier connected and packaged runs failed after Candidate preservation because cleanup requested authority after terminal release. Their failures are retained. The paired Runner/Git cleanup repair and fresh connected proof are required before merging. No live provider execution, completed scheduler, conversational head, Slack integration, installed release or authentic showcase is established by these component tests.\n",
